# Source integrity manifest — AD&D Core Rules 2.0
#
# Decided by ticket 02: the sources are NOT version-controlled, they are hashed.
# Git solves change; these files never change. What they need is IDENTITY —
# proof that the pipeline ran over these exact bytes.
#
# This matters because ticket 03 established that at least two byte-different
# DMG variants are in circulation, and that this corpus is PRE-ERRATA (TSR
# issued official PHB/DMG corrections the CD does not contain). Without these
# hashes, "the DMG" is an ambiguous phrase.
#
# A SHA-256 is a fingerprint, not the content — publishing it distributes
# nothing and lets anyone holding the same CD verify they hold the same material.
#
# Paths are relative to the sources root and are recorded as they were on the
# machine that generated this file; the hashes are what identify the material.
# Verify with:  sha256sum -c sources.sha256
#
